Rule 2 (the last two dimensions of the input tensor a must be equal to form square matrices)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 2 ∧ shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - 1) = shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - 2)
>>
Rule 3 (the input tensor a must have a float, integer, or complex data type)
{v_1 : tensor} |= 1 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 10
>>
Rule 4 (all dimensions of the input tensor a must be positive)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) > 0
>>
Rule 6 (if the exponent n is negative, the matrix a must not be a zero matrix)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= if v_2 < 0 then min(v_1) ≠ 0 ∨ max(v_1) ≠ 0
>>
Rule 8 (for negative powers, the input matrix a must have a floating-point or complex data type)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= if v_2 < 0 then 6 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 10
>>
Rule 9 (the input matrix a must have a positive size in its last dimension)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 2 ∧ shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - 1) ≥ 1
>>
Rule 12 (all dimensions of the input tensor a must have a size of at least 1)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) ≥ 1
>>
Rule 15 (the size of the square matrix must be greater than zero)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 2 ∧ shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - 1) > 0
>>
Rule 17 (batch dimensions of input tensor a must have positive sizes)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) > 2 then ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 3] : shape(v_1, i) > 0
>>
Rule 20 (if exponent is zero, the input tensor must still be at least 2-dimensional)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= if v_2 = 0 then ndim(v_1) ≥ 2
>>
Rule 21 (for 3-dimensional tensor input, the second and third dimensions must be equal)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) = 3 then shape(v_1, 1) = shape(v_1, 2)
>>
Rule 22 (for 4-dimensional tensor input, the third and fourth dimensions must be equal)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) = 4 then shape(v_1, 2) = shape(v_1, 3)
>>
Rule 23 (if the exponent is negative, the size of the square matrix must be at least 1)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= if v_2 < 0 then shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - 1) ≥ 1
